        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Stain when the wood surface — not the air — is between 50 and 90 degrees, ideally 60 to 80 in the shade. Start once the morning dew has gone, stop early enough that the finish has three to four hours before the evening dew, and make sure the overnight lows stay above 50 for the next two nights.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Follow the shade around the deck, keep an infrared thermometer in your pocket, and treat a 40 percent chance of afternoon storms as a reason to prep today and stain tomorrow. The product on the can matters far less than the four hours you choose to apply it in.
          </p>
        </div>

